\section{How the tile code is built}{

The EEA reference grid codes a cell as its size followed by its lower-left
coordinate expressed in units of that size, in EPSG:3035. A 100 km tile whose
corner sits at 4 000 000 m east and 2 200 000 m north is therefore \code{E40N22}.
The arithmetic is the documented coding system; \strong{the exact filename prefix
CLMS puts in front of it was not verified}, so match on the \code{E..N..} part
when you browse the download list.
}

